A||||8||Fiero_24||What differences are there on the 2.8 - 85,86 & 87,88||||1||
Z||000000||Fiero_24||10-15-2001||05:49 PM||||I am putting a rebuilt 86 2.8 (with lots of mods) in my 87GT.  Today I realized I ordered the wrong oil pan (I ordered the 87), and would like to know if there is anything else I should watch out for while doing this rebuild.  I pick the motor up on Friday from the shop to start the swap this weekend.  Any info would be helpful.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/driverside41.jpg"> <BR>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||10-16-2001||10:02 PM||||88 EGR tubes are different and they also didnt have coil/alternator fans.  Other than that I'm not much help  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Steve Normington||10-17-2001||10:42 AM||||86 is externally balanced, 87 may be internally balanced. Does your flexplate/flywheel have a big chunk of metal welded on it? If so, that is externally balanced and you can use it on the 86. Otherwise, you will need to get an externally balanced one. Also, are you using the timing cover from the 86? If the 87 oil pan is wrong, the timing cover will be too.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fformula88||10-17-2001||12:27 PM||||Don't worry too much, there are very few differences between the years.  The 88's use different exhaust systems... the y pipe is a little different but I believe the headers are identical.  The 88's also have different engine mounts (the little shock absorber is gone), starting in 87 a different oil pan (mentioned) I believe a couple sensors are also different.  Check Fiero Store's sensors model years to find out which ones.  There was a change for the alternator for 88, and I think thats when they went to internal balancing, but double check on that one!  Oh, and the intake Plenum's went from Fiero stickered to Fiero engraved on the top for 87.<P>Might be more, but nothing too major!  Good luck!<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/formulasig.JPG">         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">   <P>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fiero_24||10-17-2001||12:52 PM||||Thanks for the info.  I am not sure if they internally balanced though.  The harmonic balancer is universal for all the V6 motors for the Fiero.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/driverside41.jpg"> <BR>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||10
Z||000005||Voytek||10-17-2001||02:24 PM||||Actually, Steve, the '87 is also externally balanced.  As far as I know, all Fiero 2.8's from '85 through '87 are externally balanced.  I'm not sure about the '88.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Steve Normington||10-17-2001||04:03 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Voytek:<BR><B>Actually, Steve, the '87 is also externally balanced.  As far as I know, all Fiero 2.8's from '85 through '87 are externally balanced.  I'm not sure about the '88.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I thought the switch was made mid 87 (87 1/2).<P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Fiero_24||10-17-2001||05:41 PM||||I have a mid 87 GT, and it is externally balanced.  I used the 87 Harmonic balancer on the 86 motor.  The oil pans are different from what I found out.  I took the new one (86 this time instead of an 87) to the shop for them to put on, and they said the old one would not fit (not sure why, but I am no mechanic).  <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/driverside41.jpg"> <BR>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||10
Z||000008||Fformula88||10-17-2001||06:03 PM||||Looks like 88 is the year for the new balance shafts.... this is from the Pontiac Press Kit for the 88's relating to the 2.8L engine.<P>"Reliability and durability improvements for Firebird and Fiero applications of the 2.8L V6 include a revised balance weight system for the crankshaft.  The new crankshaft is internally balanced so that no counter-weighting is needed in the flywheel, integral pulley or vibration damper.  While not reducing engine weight, this change does decrease main bearing loads and helps increase durability.<P>Firebirds and Fiero equipped with the 2.8L V-6 also feature new Multec Fuel Injectors."<BR>||||reg||1
